<rml>
<head>
	<title>Skills</title>

	<!--
		A skill tree: nodes on a grid joined by lines, a points total, and a pane describing the focused
		skill. Confirm learns it.

		The "skill_tree" model this expects:

		  SkillPoints    int     points left to spend
		  Skills         array   one row per skill:
		    Name         string  read aloud, and shown in the pane
		    X, Y         int     grid cell, column and row
		    Rank         int     ranks learned; above 0 draws the node as owned
		    MaxRank      int
		    bLocked      bool    requirements not met
		  SkillLinks     array   one row per line between two nodes:
		    X1, Y1       int     one end's cell
		    X2, Y2       int     the other end's cell
		    bLit         bool    the line leads out of an owned node
		  SelectedName   string  the pane's contents, for whichever node SelectSkill last named
		  SelectedText   string
		  SelectedNeeds  string  why it is locked; empty hides the line
		  SelectedCost   int     0 hides the line
		  SelectSkill(i) command a node was focused or hovered
		  LearnSkill(i)  command a node was clicked or confirmed

		The game owns the rules: what a node needs, what it costs, which lines light. The markup only
		draws what the model says.

		Cells are 96dp apart and a node is 64dp, so a node's centre is X * 96 + 32. Change the pitch
		in .node, .tree and the link expression together. The gap between nodes is what lets
		spatial navigation pick the node straight below rather than a diagonal neighbour.
	-->
	<link type="text/template" href="/folio/lib/lib.rml"/>

	<style>
		body { justify-content: center; align-items: center; }

		.skills { display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-items: flex-start; }

		/* Three columns and three rows of cells. Add 96dp per extra column or row. */
		.tree
		{
			position: relative;
			width: 256dp;
			height: 256dp;
			margin-right: 48dp;
		}

		.link
		{
			position: absolute;
			left: 0;
			top: 0;
			width: 100%;
			height: 100%;
			path-width: 3dp;
		}

		.node
		{
			position: absolute;
			width: 64dp;
			height: 64dp;
			box-sizing: border-box;
			border-width: 2dp;
			border-radius: 10dp;
			display: flex;
			justify-content: center;
			align-items: center;
			nav: auto;
		}

		/* The theme's focus ring matches an owned node's fill, so focus also scales the node up. */
		.node:focus-visible { transform: scale(1.12); }

		.details { width: 300dp; }
		.points  { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; margin-bottom: 16dp; }
		.details-line { margin-top: 8dp; }
	</style>
</head>

<body class="screen s-pad-xl" data-model="skill_tree">
	<div class="skills">
		<div class="tree">
			<path class="link c-dim" data-for="l : SkillLinks"
				data-class-c-accent="l.bLit"
				data-attr-d="'M ' + (l.X1 * 96 + 32) + ' ' + (l.Y1 * 96 + 32) + ' L ' + (l.X2 * 96 + 32) + ' ' + (l.Y2 * 96 + 32)"></path>

			<div class="node focusable c-text" data-for="n : Skills" autofocus
				data-attr-folio-label="n.Name"
				data-class-c-raised="!n.bLocked"
				data-class-c-sunken="n.bLocked"
				data-class-c-dim="n.bLocked"
				data-class-c-fill-accent="n.Rank &gt; 0"
				data-class-c-on-accent="n.Rank &gt; 0"
				data-style-left="n.X * 96 + 'dp'"
				data-style-top="n.Y * 96 + 'dp'"
				data-event-focus="SelectSkill(it_index)"
				data-event-mouseover="SelectSkill(it_index)"
				data-event-click="LearnSkill(it_index)">
				<span class="t-numeric">{{ n.Rank }}/{{ n.MaxRank }}</span>
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="details panel">
			<div class="panel-body">
				<div class="points">
					<span class="t-caption c-dim" data-loc="skills_points">Points</span>
					<span class="t-title t-numeric c-text">{{ SkillPoints }}</span>
				</div>
				<div class="t-heading c-text">{{ SelectedName }}</div>
				<div class="details-line t-body c-muted">{{ SelectedText }}</div>
				<div class="details-line t-label c-danger" data-if="SelectedNeeds != ''">{{ SelectedNeeds }}</div>
				<div class="details-line t-label c-accent" data-if="SelectedCost &gt; 0">
					<span data-loc="skills_cost">Cost</span> <span class="t-numeric">{{ SelectedCost }}</span>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</body>
</rml>
